The rule for k_recovery says it returns the object recovered from the reply, as canonical JSON text, or NO_OBJECT. For the input fence[ S A ], the reply is a code fence containing the sentence S and the object A. The last object inside a code fence is A, so k_recovery returns the canonical JSON of A. For the rewritten text fence[ S A ] B, the fence still contains S and A, and B is after the closing fence. The last object inside a code fence is still A, so k_recovery returns the same canonical JSON of A. Therefore the answer is unchanged.